        <mxCell id="lg-lnt3" parent="legend" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;fontColor=#232F3E;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=middle;" value="Local build pipeline" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="22" width="290" x="400" y="102" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ex-title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#232F3E;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:18px&quot;&gt;Design notes&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="600" x="40" y="1300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ex-1" parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;rounded=0;strokeColor=#C5CCD3;fillColor=#FFFFFF;fontColor=#232F3E;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;padding:10px 14px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.42&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;color:#1A5276&quot;&gt;1. The browser talks to Cognito directly&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:7px&quot;&gt;Cognito is a managed service: it stores passwords, sends the verification code and issues tokens. There is no auth server to run; the only code is the small Pre Sign-up trigger (note 4).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:7px&quot;&gt;The pool id and client id are public identifiers (the browser sends them on every call). The app client has no secret, so there is nothing to hide in the build.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="593" x="40" y="1342" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ex-2" parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;rounded=0;strokeColor=#C5CCD3;fillColor=#FFFFFF;fontColor=#232F3E;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;padding:10px 14px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.42&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;color:#1A5276&quot;&gt;2. config.json wires the environment&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:7px&quot;&gt;The deploy script writes &lt;b&gt;config.json&lt;/b&gt; with region, pool id and client id from Terraform outputs. The same build serves any environment.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:7px&quot;&gt;If those values are empty the client silently falls back to in-memory fake accounts (DD-015). Check the published file after every deploy.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="593" x="653" y="1342" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ex-3" parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;rounded=0;strokeColor=#C5CCD3;fillColor=#FFFFFF;fontColor=#232F3E;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;padding:10px 14px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.42&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;color:#1A5276&quot;&gt;3. Terraform provisions, a script releases&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:7px&quot;&gt;Terraform owns the bucket, CloudFront, the user pool, the app client, the trigger and name check Lambdas (with the public Function URL) and the names table, and exports the ids. The deploy script uploads the build and &lt;code&gt;config.json&lt;/code&gt; and invalidates the cache.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:7px&quot;&gt;The game server (ALB + Fargate) is planned; the client will keep using Cognito for sign-in.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="593" x="1267" y="1342" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ex-4" parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;rounded=0;strokeColor=#C5CCD3;fillColor=#FFFFFF;fontColor=#232F3E;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;padding:10px 14px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.42&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;color:#1A5276&quot;&gt;4. Session, names and password reset&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:7px&quot;&gt;The browser stores only the Cognito &lt;b&gt;refresh token&lt;/b&gt; and the email (PlayerPrefs, IndexedDB in WebGL); ID and access tokens stay in memory. Any script on the page could read it: the page loads only the game and the Unity loader, and log out revokes the token (DD-019).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:7px&quot;&gt;Wizard names are reserved by the Pre Sign-up Lambda with a conditional DynamoDB write (DD-018). Guests are checked against those names by a public read-only Function URL (DD-021). Password reset uses the Cognito forgot-password codes (DD-020).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="593" x="40" y="1582" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
